   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Biomass percentage: 6.68%\n",
      "Abundance percentage: 7.09%\n",
      "Gear percentage: 70.32%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| include: false\n",
    "# Load the data\n",
    "all_merged = pd.read_parquet(\"Final/merged_all_final.parquet\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Strict usable-info check: exclude nulls and placeholder-like text values\n",
    "def has_info(series):\n",
    "    vals = series.astype('string').str.strip().str.lower()\n",
    "    return ~(series.isna() | vals.isin(['', 'nan', 'none', '<na>']))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate biomass percentage\n",
    "biomass_pct = (\n",
    "    (has_info(all_merged['biomass']) & has_info(all_merged['areaSampled'])).sum() / len(all_merged)\n",
    ") * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate abundance percentage (both individualCount AND areaSampled must be truly usable)\n",
    "abundance_pct = (\n",
    "    (has_info(all_merged['individualCount']) & has_info(all_merged['areaSampled'])).sum() / len(all_merged)\n",
    ") * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate gear percentage\n",
    "gear_pct = (all_merged['gear'].notna().sum() / len(all_merged)) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display results\n",
    "print(f\"Biomass percentage: {biomass_pct:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Abundance percentage: {abundance_pct:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Gear percentage: {gear_pct:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "c22ecfc6-1902-4b9c-8e52-38202a1c9205",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "The records in BENTH-MARC have varying degrees of associated information about biomass, occurrence metrics and sampling gear (@fig-panelmap a-c). We have considered only records with information about both biomass or number of individuals and sampling area to be true biomass or abundance records, as no standardization methods can be applied on records where only one of these is known. Stations with full biomass coverage and abundance data are mainly located in the Barents Sea, Norwegian Sea, Chukchi Sea and Laptev Sea. In terms of the number of records, 6.7% have biomass data and 7.1% have abundance data. Since stations can have a combination of records with and without biomass coverage as well as a combination of records with different types of occurrence metrics, the categories partial (biomass coverage) and mixed (occurrence metrics) are displayed in the maps (@fig-panelmap a-b). In addition, 70.3% of the records have associated information about sampling gear (@fig-panelmap c). "
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Markdown(\n",
    "    f\"The records in BENTH-MARC have varying degrees of associated information about biomass, occurrence metrics and sampling gear (@fig-panelmap a-c). We have considered only records with information about \" \n",
    "    f\"both biomass or number of individuals and sampling area to be true biomass or abundance records, as no standardization methods can be applied on records where only one of these is known. \" \n",
    "    f\"Stations with full biomass coverage and abundance data are \"\n",
    "    f\"mainly located in the Barents Sea, Norwegian Sea, Chukchi Sea and Laptev Sea. In terms of the number of records, {biomass_pct:.1f}% have biomass data and {abundance_pct:.1f}% have abundance data. \" \n",
    "    f\"Since stations can have a combination of records with and without biomass coverage as well as a combination of records with different types of occurrence metrics, the categories partial (biomass coverage) \"\n",
    "    f\"and mixed (occurrence metrics) are displayed in the maps (@fig-panelmap a-b). In addition, {gear_pct:.1f}% of the records have associated information about sampling gear (@fig-panelmap c). \"\n",
    "))"
   ]
  },
