   ],
   "source": [
    "#| include: false\n",
    "# Summarize records and taxa by largeMarineEcosystem\n",
    "source_df = all_merged if 'all_merged' in globals() else pd.read_parquet('Final/merged_all_final.parquet')\n",
    "\n",
    "lme_col = 'largeMarineEcosystem'\n",
    "taxa_col = 'acceptedAphiaID' if 'acceptedAphiaID' in source_df.columns else 'aphiaID'\n",
    "\n",
    "tmp = source_df[[lme_col, taxa_col]].copy()\n",
    "tmp[lme_col] = tmp[lme_col].fillna('Outside Arctic LME coverage').astype(str).str.strip()\n",
    "tmp = tmp[tmp[lme_col].ne('Outside Arctic LME coverage')]\n",
    "\n",
    "lme_stats = (\n",
    "    tmp.groupby(lme_col, dropna=False)\n",
    "       .agg(records=(lme_col, 'size'), unique_taxa=(taxa_col, 'nunique'))\n",
    "       .reset_index()\n",
    "       .rename(columns={lme_col: 'LME'})\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "highest_records = lme_stats.loc[lme_stats['records'].idxmax(), ['LME', 'records']]\n",
    "highest_taxa = lme_stats.loc[lme_stats['unique_taxa'].idxmax(), ['LME', 'unique_taxa']]\n",
    "\n",
    "lme_sorted = lme_stats.sort_values('records', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "top2_pct = lme_sorted.head(2)['records'].sum() / lme_sorted['records'].sum() * 100\n",
    "bottom5_pct = lme_sorted.tail(5)['records'].sum() / lme_sorted['records'].sum() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Highest number of records:\")\n",
    "display(highest_records.to_frame().T)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Highest number of taxa:\")\n",
    "display(highest_taxa.to_frame().T)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Top 2 LMEs account for {top2_pct:.1f}% of all records.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Bottom 5 LMEs account for {bottom5_pct:.1f}% of all records.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7461ec6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Technical validation\n",
    "\n",
    "With more than two million records in the database, manual validation of all records has not been feasible. An effort has been made to exclude stations that have high coordinate uncertainty or that appear on land, as described above (see 'Data cleaning'). An important step in the creation of the database is the application of taxonomic filters to separate benthos from irrelevant taxa, such as terrestrial, extinct and pelagic. The taxonomic filters have been validated with WoRMS' functional groups [@wormsfu] to ensure their accuracy. Only non-benthic taxa were kept in the taxonomic filters and the taxa that could not be validated using WoRMS' functional groups were validated manually. The nomenclature, taxonomic status, rank and classification of all taxa in BENTH-MARC have been validated using WoRMS. Duplicated records were removed, and erroneous year entries have been corrected. \n",
    "\n",
    "In BENTH-MARC, we have not intended to set a high bar for the requirement of metadata. The intention was to collect publicly available records of Arctic metazoan benthos in one database, and it is up to every user to decide which types of records that are applicable in their work. \n",
    "\n",
    "# Usage notes\n",
    "\n",
    "The data in BENTH-MARC come with certain qualities that need to be accounted for when applying the data on larger-scale analyses. While @fig-panelmap can help inform the user on the suitable selection of data for a certain scope, there is also an inherent patchiness in the data that the user needs to be aware of. As with any biodiversity data, the data are unevenly distributed over regions, habitat types and depths and the sampling focus has shifted over time. These characteristics are described below. Furthermore, the varying levels of taxonomic resolution in the data can lead to a need for normalizing the records prior to making comparisons (@fig-tax_resolution). "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "9e7380af-d65f-4db1-9b9e-3e6f5e1b496a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "While the spatial distribution of stations across Arctic LMEs can be seen in @fig-map_stations, @fig-lme shows an overview of the number of records and taxa per LME. Sampling effort in terms of number of records varies considerably between LMEs, with 80.4% of the total number of available records having been collected in the two most well-sampled LMEs; the Norwegian Sea and Barents Sea. The availability of public records is significantly lower in the remaining LMEs, and the five most records-poor LMEs East Siberian Sea, Northern Canadian Archipelago, Faroe Plateau, West Bering Sea, and Iceland contribute with merely 0.8% of the total number of records. In terms of available records, the Norwegian Sea is the most well-sampled LME, while Barents Sea has higher numbers of unique taxa. Iceland stands out in terms of having a low number of records but a disproportionally high number of taxa. While the large variation in number of records and taxa across LMEs partly reflects sampling effort and taxon richness, it is also heavily influenced by the size of the LME, its depth range and differences in data sharing practices. "
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Markdown(\n",
    "    f\"While the spatial distribution of stations across Arctic LMEs can be seen in @fig-map_stations, @fig-lme shows an overview of the number of records and taxa per LME. Sampling effort in terms of number of \"\n",
    "    f\"records varies considerably between LMEs, with {top2_pct:.1f}% of the total \"\n",
    "    f\"number of available records having been collected in the two most well-sampled LMEs; the Norwegian Sea and Barents Sea. \"\n",
    "    f\"The availability of public records is significantly lower in the remaining LMEs, and the five most records-poor LMEs East Siberian Sea, Northern Canadian Archipelago, Faroe Plateau, West Bering Sea, and Iceland \" \n",
    "    f\"contribute with merely {bottom5_pct:.1f}% of the total number of records. \"\n",
    "    f\"In terms of available records, the Norwegian Sea is the most well-sampled LME, while Barents Sea has higher numbers of unique taxa. Iceland stands out in terms of having a low number of records but a disproportionally high number of taxa. \"\n",
    "    f\"While the large variation in number of records and taxa across LMEs partly reflects sampling effort and taxon richness, it is also heavily influenced by the size of the LME, its depth range and differences in data sharing practices. \"\n",
    "))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 44,
   "id": "2a65d63e-7cdc-4312-9075-78fc558351fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x1000 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| fig-pos: \"H\"\n",
    "#| label: fig-lme\n",
    "#| fig-cap: \"Number of records (left side) and taxa (right side) of benthic invertebrates in the BENTH-MARC database per Arctic Large Marine Ecosystem. The proportion of species-level data is indicated in teal and by numbers in the bar plot, while grey indicates data on other taxonomic levels. \"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load data\n",
    "df_main = pd.read_parquet('Final/merged_all_final.parquet')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Standardize columns and required fields\n",
    "df_main.columns = [c.strip() for c in df_main.columns]\n",
    "lme_col = 'largeMarineEcosystem'\n",
    "accepted_col = 'acceptedAphiaID'\n",
    "rank_col = 'taxonRank'\n",
    "\n",
    "required_cols = [lme_col, accepted_col, rank_col]\n",
    "missing = [c for c in required_cols if c not in df_main.columns]\n",
    "if missing:\n",
    "    raise KeyError(f\"Required column(s) missing: {missing}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clean key fields\n",
    "df_main[accepted_col] = pd.to_numeric(df_main[accepted_col], errors='coerce')\n",
    "df_main[lme_col] = df_main[lme_col].fillna('Outside Arctic LME coverage')\n",
    "df_main[lme_col] = df_main[lme_col].astype(str).str.replace(r'\\s*LME\\s*$', '', regex=True)\n",
    "rank_norm = df_main[rank_col].astype(str).str.strip().str.upper()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Records split by species vs other ranks per LME\n",
    "total_records = df_main.groupby(lme_col, dropna=False).size().reset_index(name='records_total')\n",
    "species_records = (\n",
    "    df_main.loc[rank_norm.eq('SPECIES')]\n",
    "          .groupby(lme_col, dropna=False)\n",
    "          .size()\n",
    "          .reset_index(name='records_species')\n",
    ")\n",
    "records = pd.merge(total_records, species_records, on=lme_col, how='left').fillna({'records_species': 0})\n",
    "records['records_species'] = records['records_species'].astype(int)\n",
    "records['records_other'] = records['records_total'] - records['records_species']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Unique AphiaID split using any-species appearance within each LME\n",
    "flags = (\n",
    "    df_main.dropna(subset=[accepted_col])\n",
    "          .assign(_is_species=rank_norm.eq('SPECIES'))\n",
    "          .groupby([lme_col, accepted_col], dropna=False)['_is_species']\n",
    "          .any()\n",
    "          .reset_index(name='is_species')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "unique_total = (\n",
    "    flags.groupby(lme_col, dropna=False)[accepted_col]\n",
    "         .nunique()\n",
    "         .reset_index(name='unique_total')\n",
    ")\n",
    "unique_species = (\n",
    "    flags.loc[flags['is_species']]\n",
    "         .groupby(lme_col, dropna=False)[accepted_col]\n",
    "         .nunique()\n",
    "         .reset_index(name='unique_species')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "unique_ids = pd.merge(unique_total, unique_species, on=lme_col, how='left').fillna({'unique_species': 0})\n",
    "unique_ids['unique_species'] = unique_ids['unique_species'].astype(int)\n",
    "unique_ids['unique_other'] = unique_ids['unique_total'] - unique_ids['unique_species']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Merge all metrics\n",
    "metrics = pd.merge(\n",
    "    records[[lme_col, 'records_total', 'records_species', 'records_other']],\n",
    "    unique_ids[[lme_col, 'unique_total', 'unique_species', 'unique_other']],\n",
    "    on=lme_col,\n",
    "    how='outer'\n",
    ").fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "for c in ['records_total', 'records_species', 'records_other', 'unique_total', 'unique_species', 'unique_other']:\n",
    "    metrics[c] = metrics[c].astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort LMEs by total records\n",
    "order_all_lmes = metrics.sort_values('records_total', ascending=False)[lme_col].tolist()\n",
    "plot_df = metrics.set_index(lme_col).loc[order_all_lmes].reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Colors\n",
    "species_color = '#9DC8D2'\n",
    "other_color = '#E0E0E0'\n",
    "species_label_color = mcolors.to_hex(np.array(mcolors.to_rgb(species_color)) * 0.55)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Overall species shares\n",
    "records_species_pct_lme = 100 * plot_df['records_species'].sum() / max(plot_df['records_total'].sum(), 1)\n",
    "unique_species_pct_lme = 100 * plot_df['unique_species'].sum() / max(plot_df['unique_total'].sum(), 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build mirrored stacked plot\n",
    "fig, (ax_left, ax_right) = plt.subplots(\n",
    "    ncols=2,\n",
    "    figsize=(12, max(6, int(len(order_all_lmes) * 0.56))),\n",
    "    gridspec_kw={'width_ratios': [1, 1]}\n",
    " )\n",
    "\n",
    "y = np.arange(len(plot_df))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Left: records (negative)\n",
    "ax_left.barh(y, -plot_df['records_species'], color=species_color, label='Species', height=0.68)\n",
    "ax_left.barh(y, -plot_df['records_other'], left=-plot_df['records_species'], color=other_color, label='Other ranks', height=0.68)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Right: unique taxa (positive)\n",
    "ax_right.barh(y, plot_df['unique_species'], color=species_color, label='Species', height=0.68)\n",
    "ax_right.barh(y, plot_df['unique_other'], left=plot_df['unique_species'], color=other_color, label='Other ranks', height=0.68)\n",
    "\n",
    "left_max = float(plot_df['records_total'].max())\n",
    "right_max = float(plot_df['unique_total'].max())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Axes styling\n",
    "ax_left.set_xlabel('Number of records', fontsize=18)\n",
    "ax_left.set_xlim(-left_max * 1.36, 0)\n",
    "ax_left.spines['right'].set_visible(False)\n",
    "ax_left.spines['top'].set_visible(False)\n",
    "ax_left.xaxis.set_major_formatter(FuncFormatter(lambda x, pos: f'{int(abs(x)):,}'))\n",
    "ax_left.xaxis.set_major_locator(MaxNLocator(nbins=4, prune='both'))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax_right.set_xlabel('Number of unique taxa', fontsize=18)\n",
    "ax_right.set_xlim(0, right_max * 1.22)\n",
    "ax_right.spines['left'].set_visible(False)\n",
    "ax_right.spines['top'].set_visible(False)\n",
    "ax_right.xaxis.set_major_formatter(FuncFormatter(lambda x, pos: f'{int(x):,}'))\n",
    "ax_right.xaxis.set_major_locator(MaxNLocator(nbins=4, prune='both'))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Gridlines\n",
    "ax_left.grid(axis='y', color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=0.5, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax_right.grid(axis='y', color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=0.5, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Y labels\n",
    "ax_left.set_yticks(y)\n",
    "ax_left.set_yticklabels(order_all_lmes, fontsize=17)\n",
    "ax_right.set_yticks(y)\n",
    "ax_right.set_yticklabels([])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Draw to get renderer for fit checks\n",
    "fig.canvas.draw()\n",
    "renderer = fig.canvas.get_renderer()\n",
    "\n",
    "def text_fits_segment(ax, text, x_center, y_center, seg_width, pad_px=8, fontsize=17, fontweight='bold'):\n",
    "    tmp = ax.text(x_center, y_center, text, fontsize=fontsize, fontweight=fontweight, alpha=0.0)\n",
    "    bb = tmp.get_window_extent(renderer=renderer)\n",
    "    tmp.remove()\n",
    "\n",
    "    x0 = ax.transData.transform((x_center - seg_width / 2.0, y_center))[0]\n",
    "    x1 = ax.transData.transform((x_center + seg_width / 2.0, y_center))[0]\n",
    "    seg_px = abs(x1 - x0)\n",
    "    return bb.width <= max(0, seg_px - pad_px)\n",
    "\n",
    "left_outside_offset = left_max * 0.12\n",
    "right_outside_offset = right_max * 0.10\n",
    "\n",
    "# Species labels only: inside if fit, otherwise outside with connector lines\n",
    "for i, row in plot_df.iterrows():\n",
    "    rec_species = int(row['records_species'])\n",
    "    uniq_species = int(row['unique_species'])\n",
    "\n",
    "    rec_species_str = f\"{rec_species:,}\"\n",
    "    uniq_species_str = f\"{uniq_species:,}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    rec_species_center = -rec_species / 2.0\n",
    "    uniq_species_center = uniq_species / 2.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    if rec_species > 0 and text_fits_segment(ax_left, rec_species_str, rec_species_center, y[i], rec_species):\n",
    "        ax_left.text(\n",
    "            rec_species_center, y[i], rec_species_str,\n",
    "            ha='center', va='center', fontsize=14,\n",
    "            color=species_label_color, fontweight='bold'\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        rec_label_x = -rec_species - left_outside_offset\n",
    "        ax_left.annotate(\n",
    "            rec_species_str,\n",
    "            xy=(rec_species_center, y[i]),\n",
    "            xytext=(rec_label_x, y[i]),\n",
    "            ha='right', va='center',\n",
    "            fontsize=14, color=species_label_color, fontweight='bold',\n",
    "            arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='-', color=species_label_color, lw=1.1, shrinkA=0, shrinkB=0)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    if uniq_species > 0 and text_fits_segment(ax_right, uniq_species_str, uniq_species_center, y[i], uniq_species):\n",
    "        ax_right.text(\n",
    "            uniq_species_center, y[i], uniq_species_str,\n",
    "            ha='center', va='center', fontsize=14,\n",
    "            color=species_label_color, fontweight='bold'\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        uniq_label_x = uniq_species + right_outside_offset\n",
    "        ax_right.annotate(\n",
    "            uniq_species_str,\n",
    "            xy=(uniq_species_center, y[i]),\n",
    "            xytext=(uniq_label_x, y[i]),\n",
    "            ha='left', va='center',\n",
    "            fontsize=14, color=species_label_color, fontweight='bold',\n",
    "            arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='-', color=species_label_color, lw=1.1, shrinkA=0, shrinkB=0)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Species share annotations\n",
    "ax_left.text(\n",
    "    0.02, 1.02,\n",
    "    f\"Species share: {records_species_pct_lme:.1f}%\",\n",
    "    transform=ax_left.transAxes,\n",
    "    fontsize=14,\n",
    "    ha='left',\n",
    "    va='bottom'\n",
    " )\n",
    "ax_right.text(\n",
    "    0.98, 1.02,\n",
    "    f\"Species share: {unique_species_pct_lme:.1f}%\",\n",
    "    transform=ax_right.transAxes,\n",
    "    fontsize=14,\n",
    "    ha='right',\n",
    "    va='bottom'\n",
    " )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Shared legend\n",
    "legend_handles = [\n",
    "    Patch(facecolor=species_color, edgecolor='none', label='Species'),\n",
    "    Patch(facecolor=other_color, edgecolor='none', label='Other taxonomic levels')\n",
    "]\n",
    "fig.legend(\n",
    "    handles=legend_handles,\n",
    "    loc='upper center',\n",
    "    ncol=2,\n",
    "    frameon=False,\n",
    "    bbox_to_anchor=(0.66, 0.99),\n",
    "    fontsize=18\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Layout and save\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.subplots_adjust(top=0.86, wspace=0.02)\n",
    "plt.savefig('Figures/lme_records_taxa_all.png', dpi=220, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
