     "text": [
      "Percentage from 1600s: 0.0000000000%\n",
      "Percentage from 1700s: 0.0007620103%\n",
      "Percentage from 1800s: 0.9%\n",
      "Percentage before 2000: 15.0%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# | include: false\n",
    "# Calculate percentage of records from 1700s and before 2000\n",
    "\n",
    "source_df = pd.read_parquet('Final/merged_all_final.parquet')\n",
    "\n",
    "df_year = source_df[['year']].copy()\n",
    "df_year['year'] = pd.to_numeric(df_year['year'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove NaN years\n",
    "df_year_valid = df_year.dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "total_records_year = len(df_year_valid)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Records from 1600s (1600-1699)\n",
    "records_1600s = ((df_year_valid['year'] >= 1600) & (df_year_valid['year'] < 1700)).sum()\n",
    "pct_1600s = (records_1600s / total_records_year * 100) if total_records_year > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Records from 1700s (1700-1799)\n",
    "records_1700s = ((df_year_valid['year'] >= 1700) & (df_year_valid['year'] < 1800)).sum()\n",
    "pct_1700s = (records_1700s / total_records_year * 100) if total_records_year > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Records from 1800s (1800-1899)\n",
    "records_1800s = ((df_year_valid['year'] >= 1800) & (df_year_valid['year'] < 1900)).sum()\n",
    "pct_1800s_valid = (records_1800s / total_records_year * 100) if total_records_year > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Records before 2000 (year < 2000)\n",
    "records_before_2000 = (df_year_valid['year'] < 2000).sum()\n",
    "pct_before_2000_valid = (records_before_2000 / total_records_year * 100) if total_records_year > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Percentage from 1600s: {pct_1600s:.10f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Percentage from 1700s: {pct_1700s:.10f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Percentage from 1800s: {pct_1800s_valid:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Percentage before 2000: {pct_before_2000_valid:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 57,
   "id": "bc122926-5af3-4121-afb7-6611f1a10e29",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "The data in BENTH-MARC span back all the way to the 1700s, but only 1% of the records originate from before the 20th century (@fig-time). The vast majority of the data are recent, with 85% of the records being sampled after year 2000. Apart from the increasing number of records over time, there also appears to have been a shift in focus from sampling only one or a few taxonomic groups at a time to more community-oriented sampling. @fig-time a) shows the development over time from almost exclusively single-phylum stations to a clear downward trend in single-phylum stations since around year 2000. The relative increase over the previous three years might be related to a time lag in the identification of taxa in more comprehensive, community-based studies. The overall reduction in single-phylum stations can be interpreted as a shift in research focus from taxonomy to ecology. Together, the limited availability of historic data and the shift in study focus limit the applicability of the data in long-term comparisons. There are however examples of long-term comparisons in the literature that have successfully used publicly available data to compare species distributions over time, such as Calvin et al. 2024 [@calvet2024]. "
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "display(Markdown(\n",
    "    f\"The data in BENTH-MARC span back all the way to the 1700s, but only {(pct_1800s_valid + pct_1700s + pct_1600s):.0f}% of the records originate from before the 20th century (@fig-time). \"\n",
    "    f\"The vast majority of the data are recent, with {100-pct_before_2000_valid:.0f}% of the records being sampled after year 2000. \"\n",
    "    f\"Apart from the increasing number of records over time, there also appears to have been a shift in focus from sampling only one or a few taxonomic groups at a time to \"\n",
    "    f\"more community-oriented sampling. @fig-time a) shows the development over time from almost exclusively single-phylum stations to a clear downward trend in single-phylum stations since around year 2000. \" \n",
    "    f\"The relative increase over the previous three years might be related to a time lag in the identification of taxa in more comprehensive, community-based studies. \" \n",
    "    f\"The overall reduction in single-phylum stations can be interpreted as a shift in research focus from taxonomy to ecology. \"\n",
    "    f\"Together, the limited availability of historic data and the shift in study focus limit the applicability of the data in long-term comparisons. \"\n",
    "    f\"There are however examples of long-term comparisons in the literature that have successfully used publicly available data to compare species distributions over time, such as Calvin et al. 2024 [@calvet2024]. \"\n",
    "))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a669bd1-8645-4a8f-96ea-075f660f7d94",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "@fig-time b) shows the six most common phyla among single-phylum stations, in decreasing order of number of sample stations. Cnidaria, Porifera, Arthropoda, Mollusca and Echinodermata have been the focus at more than 10,000 stations each, whereas Annelida has been the focus of fewer targeted studies. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 78,
   "id": "10820223-d208-4391-b4d6-39ed19b0dae9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1100x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Plot dual-axis chart using all_merged.parquet and all_stations.parquet\n",
    "# Shows: records per year + proportion of single-phylum stations per year\n",
    "#| fig-pos: \"H\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load source data\n",
    "all_merged_df = pd.read_parquet('Final/merged_all_final.parquet')\n",
    "all_stations_df = pd.read_parquet('Final/all_stations.parquet')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Shared station-defining columns available in both parquet files\n",
    "station_cols = ['datasetKey', 'decimalLatitudeStart', 'decimalLongitudeStart', 'year']\n",
    "required_merged = station_cols + ['phylum']\n",
    "missing_merged = [c for c in required_merged if c not in all_merged_df.columns]\n",
    "missing_stations = [c for c in station_cols if c not in all_stations_df.columns]\n",
    "if missing_merged:\n",
    "    raise KeyError(f\"Missing required column(s) in all_merged.parquet: {missing_merged}\")\n",
    "if missing_stations:\n",
    "    raise KeyError(f\"Missing required column(s) in all_stations.parquet: {missing_stations}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare station universe from all_stations (denominator)\n",
    "stations = all_stations_df[station_cols].copy()\n",
    "stations['year'] = pd.to_numeric(stations['year'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "stations['decimalLatitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(stations['decimalLatitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "stations['decimalLongitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(stations['decimalLongitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "stations = stations.dropna(subset=station_cols)\n",
    "stations['year'] = stations['year'].astype(int)\n",
    "stations = stations.drop_duplicates(station_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare merged records and normalize phylum\n",
    "merged = all_merged_df[required_merged].copy()\n",
    "merged['year'] = pd.to_numeric(merged['year'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "merged['decimalLatitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(merged['decimalLatitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "merged['decimalLongitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(merged['decimalLongitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "merged = merged.dropna(subset=station_cols)\n",
    "merged['year'] = merged['year'].astype(int)\n",
    "merged['phylum_norm'] = merged['phylum'].astype(str).str.strip().str.lower()\n",
    "merged_valid = merged[~merged['phylum_norm'].isin(['', 'nan', 'none', '<na>'])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Records per year (bars)\n",
    "records_per_year = merged.groupby('year').size().reset_index(name='RecordCount')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Number of unique phyla per station-year from all_merged\n",
    "station_phyla = (\n",
    "    merged_valid.groupby(station_cols, as_index=False)['phylum_norm']\n",
    "              .nunique()\n",
    "              .rename(columns={'phylum_norm': 'n_phyla'})\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Join to all stations so denominator truly comes from all_stations\n",
    "station_summary = stations.merge(station_phyla, on=station_cols, how='left')\n",
    "station_summary['n_phyla'] = station_summary['n_phyla'].fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "single_per_year = (\n",
    "    station_summary.groupby('year', as_index=False)\n",
    "                   .agg(\n",
    "                       TotalStations=('n_phyla', 'size'),\n",
    "                       SingleStations=('n_phyla', lambda s: int((s == 1).sum()))\n",
    "                   )\n",
    ")\n",
    "single_per_year['Prop_Single'] = np.where(\n",
    "    single_per_year['TotalStations'] > 0,\n",
    "    single_per_year['SingleStations'] / single_per_year['TotalStations'],\n",
    "    np.nan\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Final plotting frame\n",
    "plot_df_sorted = (\n",
    "    records_per_year.merge(\n",
    "        single_per_year[['year', 'TotalStations', 'Prop_Single']],\n",
    "        on='year',\n",
    "        how='left'\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    .sort_values('year')\n",
    "    .rename(columns={'year': 'Year'})\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Colors per existing style\n",
    "color_prop = '#3F7B89'\n",
    "color_prop_low_n = \"#FFFFFF\"  # marker color for years with <10 stations\n",
    "color_recs = '#815A7F'\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(11, 6))\n",
    "ax1 = plt.gca()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bars on secondary axis\n",
    "ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n",
    "ax2.bar(plot_df_sorted['Year'], plot_df_sorted['RecordCount'], color=color_recs, alpha=0.35, width=0.85, label='Records per year', zorder=1)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Number of records per year', color=color_recs, fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax2.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor=color_recs)\n",
    "ax2.set_yscale('log')\n",
    "ax2.yaxis.set_major_formatter(FuncFormatter(lambda x, pos: f'{x:,.0f}'))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure line/markers are drawn above bars in twin-axis rendering\n",
    "ax1.set_zorder(ax2.get_zorder() + 1)\n",
    "ax1.patch.set_alpha(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Line on primary axis\n",
    "sns.lineplot(\n",
    "    data=plot_df_sorted,\n",
    "    x='Year',\n",
    "    y='Prop_Single',\n",
    "    color=color_prop,\n",
    "    linewidth=2.0,\n",
    "    marker=None,\n",
    "    ax=ax1,\n",
    "    zorder=5,\n",
    "    label='_nolegend_'\n",
    " )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Markers with different colors for low station-count years\n",
    "mask_low_n = plot_df_sorted['TotalStations'] < 10\n",
    "mask_ok_n = ~mask_low_n\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.scatter(\n",
    "    plot_df_sorted.loc[mask_ok_n, 'Year'],\n",
    "    plot_df_sorted.loc[mask_ok_n, 'Prop_Single'],\n",
    "    s=28,\n",
    "    color=color_prop,\n",
    "    edgecolor='white',\n",
    "    linewidth=0.8,\n",
    "    zorder=6,\n",
    "    label='Years with >=10 stations'\n",
    " )\n",
    "ax1.scatter(\n",
    "    plot_df_sorted.loc[mask_low_n, 'Year'],\n",
    "    plot_df_sorted.loc[mask_low_n, 'Prop_Single'],\n",
    "    s=34,\n",
    "    color=color_prop_low_n,\n",
    "    edgecolor='#3F7B89',\n",
    "    linewidth=0.8,\n",
    "    zorder=7,\n",
    "    label='Years with <10 stations'\n",
    " )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Axes style\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Proportion of single-phylum stations per year', color=color_prop, fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor=color_prop)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
    "ax1.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Year', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax1.set_title('', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# More x ticks and labels\n",
    "min_year = int(plot_df_sorted['Year'].min())\n",
    "max_year = int(plot_df_sorted['Year'].max())\n",
    "ax1.set_xticks(np.arange(1770, max_year + 1, 20))\n",
    "ax1.set_xlim(1770, max_year)\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='x', labelrotation=45)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Legend\n",
    "handles1, labels1 = ax1.get_legend_handles_labels()\n",
    "ax1.legend(handles1, labels1, loc='upper left', frameon=False, fontsize=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save output\n",
    "fig_path = 'Figures/time.png'\n",
    "plt.savefig(fig_path, dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight', facecolor='white')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 66,
   "id": "6a93d6b3-c824-4a31-a70c-7eb5f987d0d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x180 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: fig-time\n",
    "#| fig-cap: \"a) The number of records of benthic invertebrates in the BENTH-MARC database over time and the proportion of single-phylum stations per year, indicating a shift in sampling focus from single-phylum stations to communities. Figure 8: b) The phyla that have most commonly been the focus of single-phylum stations.\"\n",
    "#| fig-pos: \"H\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rebase to use parquet files and same station definition as cell 60\n",
    "# Count single-phylum stations by phylum\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load source data (reuse from cell 60 if available, or reload)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    all_merged_df\n",
    "    all_stations_df\n",
    "except NameError:\n",
    "    all_merged_df = pd.read_parquet('Final/merged_all_final.parquet')\n",
    "    all_stations_df = pd.read_parquet('Final/all_stations_final.parquet')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Same station definition from cell 60\n",
    "station_cols = ['datasetKey', 'decimalLatitudeStart', 'decimalLongitudeStart', 'year']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare stations\n",
    "stations = all_stations_df[station_cols].copy()\n",
    "stations['year'] = pd.to_numeric(stations['year'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "stations['decimalLatitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(stations['decimalLatitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "stations['decimalLongitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(stations['decimalLongitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "stations = stations.dropna(subset=station_cols)\n",
    "stations['year'] = stations['year'].astype(int)\n",
    "stations = stations.drop_duplicates(station_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare merged records and normalize phylum\n",
    "merged = all_merged_df[station_cols + ['phylum']].copy()\n",
    "merged['year'] = pd.to_numeric(merged['year'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "merged['decimalLatitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(merged['decimalLatitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "merged['decimalLongitudeStart'] = pd.to_numeric(merged['decimalLongitudeStart'], errors='coerce').round(5)\n",
    "merged = merged.dropna(subset=station_cols)\n",
    "merged['year'] = merged['year'].astype(int)\n",
    "merged['phylum_norm'] = merged['phylum'].astype(str).str.strip().str.lower()\n",
    "merged_valid = merged[~merged['phylum_norm'].isin(['', 'nan', 'none', '<na>'])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count unique phyla per station\n",
    "station_phyla = (\n",
    "    merged_valid.groupby(station_cols, as_index=False)['phylum_norm']\n",
    "              .nunique()\n",
    "              .rename(columns={'phylum_norm': 'n_phyla'})\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Join to all stations\n",
    "station_summary = stations.merge(station_phyla, on=station_cols, how='left')\n",
    "station_summary['n_phyla'] = station_summary['n_phyla'].fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter to single-phylum stations only\n",
    "single_phylum_stations = station_summary[station_summary['n_phyla'] == 1].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the phylum for each single-phylum station\n",
    "single_stations_with_phyla = single_phylum_stations.merge(\n",
    "    merged_valid[station_cols + ['phylum_norm']].drop_duplicates(station_cols),\n",
    "    on=station_cols,\n",
    "    how='left',\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count stations by phylum, sorted descending\n",
    "phylum_counts = (\n",
    "    single_stations_with_phyla.groupby('phylum_norm', as_index=False).size()\n",
    "    .rename(columns={'size': 'station_count'})\n",
    "    .sort_values('station_count', ascending=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only phyla with enough stations\n",
    "min_station_count = 4000\n",
    "plot_df = phylum_counts[phylum_counts['station_count'] > min_station_count].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "if plot_df.empty:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f'No phyla have more than {min_station_count:,} stations.')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare for plotting\n",
    "labels = plot_df['phylum_norm'].tolist()\n",
    "values = plot_df['station_count'].tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build colors dynamically to match whatever phyla pass the threshold\n",
    "base_colors = ['#2C3E50', '#9DC8D2', \"#815A7F\", \"#2C3E5083\", \"#B0B37C\", \"#4C5355\", '#6C4E8A', '#3B8EA5']\n",
    "if len(base_colors) < len(values):\n",
    "    base_colors = base_colors * ((len(values) // len(base_colors)) + 1)\n",
    "colors = base_colors[:len(values)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cumulative left positions for each segment\n",
    "cum_left = np.cumsum([0] + list(values[:-1]))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot the bars\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 1.8))\n",
    "for lab, val, left, color in zip(labels, values, cum_left, colors):\n",
    "    plt.barh([0], [val], left=left, color=color, edgecolor='white', height=0.08)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if val > 0:\n",
    "        x_center = left + val / 2.0\n",
    "        count = int(val)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Calculate luminance to determine text color\n",
    "        r, g, b = [int(color.lstrip('#')[j:j+2], 16) for j in (0, 2, 4)]\n",
    "        luminance = 0.2126 * r + 0.7152 * g + 0.0722 * b\n",
    "        txt_color = 'white' if luminance < 128 else 'black'\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Add count text with thousand separators\n",
    "        text_str = f'{count:,}'\n",
    "        plt.text(\n",
    "            x_center,\n",
    "            0,\n",
    "            text_str,\n",
    "            va='center',\n",
    "            ha='center',\n",
    "            color=txt_color,\n",
    "            fontsize=12,\n",
    "            fontweight='bold',\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create legend only for plotted phyla\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import Patch\n",
    "legend_labels = [lab.capitalize() for lab in labels]\n",
    "legend_patches = [Patch(facecolor=color, edgecolor='white', linewidth=1.5) for color in colors]\n",
    "\n",
    "ax = plt.gca()\n",
    "plt.legend(\n",
    "    handles=legend_patches,\n",
    "    labels=legend_labels,\n",
    "    loc='upper center',\n",
    "    bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, 1.22),\n",
    "    ncol=min(6, len(legend_labels)),\n",
    "    frameon=False,\n",
    "    fontsize=11,\n",
    "    handleheight=0.8,\n",
    "    handlelength=0.8,\n",
    "    columnspacing=0.8,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Most common phyla among single-phylum stations', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', y=0.95)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax = plt.gca()\n",
    "for spine in ax.spines.values():\n",
    "    spine.set_visible(False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Customize plot with thousands formatter on x-axis\n",
    "plt.yticks([0], [''])\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Number of stations', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.xaxis.set_major_formatter(FuncFormatter(lambda x, pos: f'{int(x):,}'))\n",
    "plt.xticks(fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Adjust layout and save the figure\n",
    "plt.subplots_adjust(top=0.7)\n",
    "fig_path = 'Figures/single_phylum.png'\n",
    "plt.savefig(fig_path, dpi=200, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
